UID:rehearsals-for-a-revolution-56802@pathe.ch
DESCRIPTION:Through five portraits of relatives and mentors\, five express
 ions of resistance\, Pegah Ahangarani sketches her life story. Drawing fro
 m personal archives\, home videos\, street protests footage\, newspapers\,
  and recorded voices\, she retraces more than 40 years of Iran’s history
 . From the early days of 1979\, until the war that began in 2026\, she pie
 ces together intimate and collective memories\, forming the portrait of a 
 country shaped by political repression and in constant hope for a revoluti
 on.
